Removed

  Earlier revisions vendored the OpenAI Agents SDK for TypeScript/JavaScript's
  `applyDiff` (packages/agents-core/src/utils/applyDiff.ts, MIT, commit
  e2cbca883dfccae90791c1e9237c15ef897a85d2) under tool-apply-patch/vendor/, on
  the assumption that one V4A implementation is like another. It is not — the
  two disagree on where a context-free `+` hunk lands, on trailing newlines, on
  CRLF, and on how far a near-miss context line may drift — so an arm that
  exists to measure Codex's contract cannot use it. Nothing from that SDK
  remains, including the operation names its `ApplyPatchOperation` used.
